config BR2_PACKAGE_QUUX_FILE_DEVICE
	bool "quux-file-device"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON
	help
	  QUUX's file device, the Linux side: the program that serves
	  the card's folders to QUUX as the pathname host HOST.  QUUX
	  writes commands into a ring in its main memory and this reads
	  them out of DDR, does each on a Linux folder, and writes the
	  answer back, through the file device's page in the fabric.
	  It also keeps QUUX's real-time clock.

	  QUUX only: its init script starts it when the card's fpgarc
	  says --machine quux, and not otherwise.

